    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0549" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.4112/94</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Howard</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                        1924</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of June 23, 1924<anchor n="26" xml:id="d383-f1"/> in which
                    you were good enough to convey to me the thanks and appreciation of His
                    Majesty’s Government for the assistance which this Government and its diplomatic
                    representative at Mexico City were able to extend during the recent crisis in
                    connection with Mr. Cummins. I furthermore note your request, on the
                    instructions of His Majesty’s Principal Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs,
                    that for the time being this Government should take charge of British interests
                    in Mexico.</p>
                <p>In reply, I beg to inform you that in the absence of a British diplomatic
                    representative in Mexico this Government will be glad to extend its appropriate
                    good offices in relation to British interests in that country. I have instructed
                    the American Ambassador at Mexico City to that effect and have directed him to
                    advise the Mexican Government of the British Government’s request.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
